Package: mstate2
Type: Package
Title: Second-Order Markov Multistate Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Josu", "Najera-Zuloaga", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "josu.najera@ehu.eus"),
    person("Mireia", "Besalu", role = "aut"),
    person("Guadalupe", "Gomez Melis", role = "aut"))
Description: Nonparametric estimation and inference for second-order Markov
    multistate models in discrete time. Provides the relative probability
    estimator (RPE) and the conditional probability estimator (CPE) of the
    1-step second-order homogeneous transition probabilities, together with
    consistent variance estimators, confidence intervals, an extension of the
    Chapman-Kolmogorov relation for n-step prediction, and evolution intervals.
    The package complements 'mstate' by adding a second-order (short-memory)
    layer to the classical first-order multistate framework. Methods are
    described in Najera-Zuloaga, Besalu and Gomez Melis (2025) and build on
    Besalu and Gomez Melis (2024) <SORT>.
